---
import WalkthroughLayout from '../../layouts/WalkthroughLayout.astro';
import ChapterCard from '../../components/ChapterCard.astro';
import TacticalBriefing from '../../components/TacticalBriefing.astro';
import AsciiMap from '../../components/AsciiMap.astro';
import BossCard from '../../components/BossCard.astro';
import ShopMatrix from '../../components/ShopMatrix.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import Tag from '../../components/Tag.astro';

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const quickJumps = [
  { "id": "ch11", "number": 11, "title": "Gran Plain (Standard Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Standard" },
  { "id": "ch12", "number": 12, "title": "Alma Mine (Alternate Prologue)", "timeline": "Prologue" },
  { "id": "ch13", "number": 13, "title": "Alistel (Alternate Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Alternate" },
  { "id": "ch14", "number": 14, "title": "Lazvil Hills (Alternate Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Alternate" },
  { "id": "ch15", "number": 15, "title": "Judgement Cliff (Alternate Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Alternate" },
  { "id": "ch16", "number": 16, "title": "Sand Fortress (Alternate Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Alternate" },
  { "id": "ch17", "number": 17, "title": "Gran Plain (Standard Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Standard" },
  { "id": "ch18", "number": 18, "title": "Granorg (Standard Chapter 1)", "timeline": "Standard" },
  { "id": "ch19", "number": 19, "title": "Granorg (Standard Chapter 2)", "timeline": "Standard" },
  { "id": "ch20", "number": 20, "title": "Underground Waterway (Standard Chapter 2)", "timeline": "Standard" }
];

const stats = {
  chapters: 10,
  nodes: 18,
  endings: 3,
  sidequests: 6,
  bosses: 5
};

const prevVol = { num: 1, title: 'Prologue & First Assignments', href: `${baseUrl}walkthrough/volume-1/` };
const nextVol = { num: 3, title: 'Celestia Alliance & Fortress Battles', href: `${baseUrl}walkthrough/volume-3/` };
---

<WalkthroughLayout
  volume={2}
  volumeTitle="Specint Espionage & Underground Passages"
  chapterRange="Chapters 11–20"
  description="Deep covert operations across Gran Plain, infiltrating Granorg via the dangerous Underground Waterways, and early boss clashes with the Shadow and Granorg guards."
  stats={stats}
  quickJumps={quickJumps}
  prevVol={prevVol}
  nextVol={nextVol}
>

  <!-- Chapter 11 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch11"
    number={11}
    title="Gran Plain (Standard Chapter 1)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="14"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      enemies={[
        { name: "Blue Flame", weakness: "Ice" },
        { name: "Goblin Foot", weakness: "Lightning" },
        { name: "Wood Goblin", weakness: "Lightning" }
      ]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap title="Gran Plain - East & South East Paths">
<pre>    Gran
   Plain E
   _______
  |       |
  |       |
  |__   __|
  ___| |__
    S     |
  _       |
   \     /
    \   /
     | |

     | |__
    /     |
   /    __|
  |    |___
  |        |
  |     ___|
  |    |

Gran Plain SE</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <p>There&#x27;s no treasure here either, so just head north to <Tag type="place">Gran Plain East</Tag>, and west to the checkpoint. Yet again, you&#x27;ll be distracted by someone in distress back east. Make sure to choose &quot;Let&#x27;s go save her now.&quot;, as this is a requirement to unlocking the [At Journey&#x27;s End] sidequest later. Either way, you&#x27;ll have to deal with the source of the disturbance.</p>

      <BossCard
        name="Sabertooth Tiger x2"
        weakness="None"
      >
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Have <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> cast <Tag type="skill">Magic Boost</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>, while <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> and she <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> the tigers into the back row. Then, use two combos of <Tag type="skill">Left Assault</Tag>, any spell, and an attack from Marco to finish them off quickly.</p>
      </BossCard>

      <p>For defeating them, you will meet <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag>, <Tag type="char">Liese</Tag>, and <Tag type="char">Vanoss</Tag>, all Beastkind of the Satyros, and the former of which who will join your party. I would recommend handing Stocke&#x27;s <Tag type="armor">Beast Skins</Tag> down to <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag>, as I&#x27;m going to purchase something new for him soon enough, anyway.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Beastkind">
        <p>Now, return west to the checkpoint where you have another decision to make. Choosing to &quot;Force your way through&quot; will unlock [A Sealed Path] ending.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Stocke&#x27;s Display">
        <p>Return to this node, even though trying to &quot;Abandon the idea&quot; will only lead to a dead end for now.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Sword Dancing">
        <p>There&#x27;s nothing we can do here for now. If you have already resolved this roadblock, then skip ahead to Chapter 17 (Gran Plain - Standard Chapter 1). Otherwise, this would be a good time to wrap up some sidequests.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Return to &quot;The Beginning&quot; node and choose to Join the Rosch Brigade. If you have at least <Tag type="gold">5300 G</Tag>, then go ahead and buy a <Tag type="weapon">Custom Lance</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag>. Head down to the <Tag type="place">First Ward</Tag> and give the <Tag type="item">2 Anti-Sleeps</Tag> you purchased earlier to the soldier on the left to complete the [Night Watch] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="weapon">Alistel Edge</Tag> (ATK+16/MAG+6, equip on <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>).</p>

      <p>Continue on with the plot as before and return to the site of the cave-in. For those who don&#x27;t remember, go west and south one screen. Then, hug the river clockwise until it turns north to where you met the spy in Standard History. At this point, the soldier is still alive, so use the barrel to blow away the rocks. Talk to the soldier to complete the [Accident in the Cave] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="key">Right-Cut Scroll</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>, though you can&#x27;t use it for now. You can either walk to <Tag type="place">Alma Mine</Tag> or use Historia to skip ahead to [The Closed Mine] node.</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 12 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch12"
    number={12}
    title="Alma Mine (Alternate Prologue)"
    timeline="Prologue"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="16"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Rosch"
      enemies={[
        { name: "Amber Leech", weakness: "Poison / Fire" },
        { name: "Basilisk", weakness: "Lightning" },
        { name: "Goblin Knight", weakness: "Poison / Lightning" }
      ]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap title="Alma Mine - Deep Mine Passages">
<pre>      _| |  ___      S - Save Point     X - Roadblock     1 - Heavy Mail
     /   |_|  4|     2 - 800 G     3 - Royal Jelly x4     4 - Healing Herb
    |   __X__|
  __|XX|_____
 |3____ S _  |
       | |_| |
       |___  |
           | |
 _____
|2   _|    | |
  | |_____/  |
  |_______   |
   _______|XX|
  |  _   _   |
  | |_| |_|  |
  |___   ___/
   ___| |_
  |  _____|
  | |

  | |__   __
  |  __| |1 |
  |X|_    | |
  |  _|   |X|
  | |____/ /
  |       /
   \_   _/
     | |</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <p>If you have resolved saving the merchant in Alternate History, then you can continue with the plot here. Don&#x27;t think about it too much. Just pretend it makes sense. Choose to &quot;Send Scouts&quot; and you will gain access to the <Tag type="place">Alma Mine</Tag>.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Duel in the Dark">
        <p>Before beginning the battle, leave the mine, and talk to the merchant outside the house there. Buy <Tag type="armor">3 Silver Mails</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>, <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>, &amp; <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag>. I&#x27;d also recommend buying <Tag type="acc">3 Pawn Studs</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>, since none of his abilities rely on strength or magic that much.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Silver Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Silver Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Alistel Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Bronze Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Pawn Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Rosch:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Custom Lance</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Silver Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Don&#x27;t worry if your levels aren&#x27;t nearly what I have, since the dungeon isn&#x27;t very long or hard. Take the left path until you find some barrels. Pull it all the way around to the right path to blow away the rocks blocking a chest which contains a <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag> (DEF+21/MDF+15/SPD-2, equip on <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>). Don&#x27;t worry about the loss of speed. Physical defense is king in this game. Return to the barrels, and blow up the nearby boulders to gain access to the next area.</p>

      <p>Go right to the fork, up, and left to find a barrel. Pull it to the right to blow up the rocks over there. After a cutscene, head left to a room with a chest which contains <Tag type="gold">800 G</Tag>. Return to where you blew up the rock, and walk up to the next area.</p>

      <p>Take either path around to a save point. Go left to a couple barrels. Pull one of them back, so you don&#x27;t end up blowing them both up at the same time. You&#x27;ll need both of them to get through the boulders. To the left is a chest which contains <Tag type="item">4 Royal Jellies</Tag>. Blow up the boulders and pull one of the barrels to the right to blow up some more. Follow the path to the right to a chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Healing Herb</Tag>.</p>

      <p>You may want to return to the save point to heal up and/or use some <Tag type="item">Royal Jellies</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>. For the next part, if you&#x27;re not going to use Raynie, then give her <Tag type="acc">Horn Charms</Tag> to <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>. In either case, you will reach the end of the mine to the north, and find what you were looking for.</p>

      <BossCard
        name="Granorg Archer x3, Light Granorgite x4"
        weakness="None"
      >
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> You&#x27;ll definitely want <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> for this fight, starting by casting <Tag type="skill">Magic Boost</Tag> on your primary magic user for this fight. Any combination of Assaults and a spell should be able to take them out. Otherwise, maybe casting <Tag type="skill">Guard Boost</Tag> would be a good idea with so many of them around. They&#x27;re not particularly dangerous, if you&#x27;ve been following the walkthrough up to now.</p>
      </BossCard>

      <p>Afterwards, everyone returns home to <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag> after a job well done.</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 13 -->
