| |_____   ____| | 2 - 1500 G
|______2| |______|
        | |</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: A New Mission">
        <p>When you regain control of <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>, you&#x27;ll be outside the tavern. Climb the stairs to the left and talk to the man all the way at the bottom. His name is <Tag type="char">Cedric</Tag> and he will give you the [A Letter to Tomorrow] sidequest. Now that the road is fixed, you have access to the left upper level of the <Tag type="place">First Ward</Tag> below. Open the two chests there which contain a <Tag type="acc">Seed Ring</Tag> (HP+10/MP+5, sell) and <Tag type="gold">1500 G</Tag>. Now, head back up to the castle.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Talk to the receptionist to the left to receive the [Engineer Recruit] sidequest. In the lower right of the <Tag type="place">1st Floor</Tag> is a woman tending to the flowers. Talk to her to receive the [A Flower of Promise] sidequest. Above her are two rooms. Enter the left room and talk to the blue soldier who wasn&#x27;t there before to receive the [Raynie the Active] &amp; [Marco the Calm] sidequests. If you completed the Accident in the Cave sidequest, then talk to him again and choose &quot;Teach it to Marco&quot; to use the <Tag type="key">Right-Cut Scroll</Tag>, so he can learn <Tag type="skill">Right Assault</Tag> for himself.</p>

      <p>Leave and enter the door to the right. Before talking to <Tag type="char">Sonja</Tag> in the infirmary, enter the <Tag type="place">Laboratory</Tag> to the left. Talk to the woman there named <Tag type="char">Meese</Tag> to receive the [Red-Letter Day] sidequest. Now go to the <Tag type="place">Infirmary</Tag> in the room to the right and talk to Sonja.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Summoned by Raul">
        <p>Head back downstairs and talk to <Tag type="char">Sonja</Tag> to advance the [Red-Letter Day] sidequest. Now&#x27;s as good a time as any to jump around time. Return to &quot;The Beginning&quot; node and talk to <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag> on the first floor. Choosing to &quot;Chase after&quot; Sonja will unlock [A Knight&#x27;s End] ending. Otherwise, choosing to &quot;Send Rosch&quot; will advance the [Red-Letter Day] sidequest.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Before turning in the sidequest, return to &quot;The Closed Mine&quot; node. Enter the house and talk to the engineer, <Tag type="char">Berman</Tag>, to advance the [Engineer Recruit] sidequest. Return to the [A New Mission] node. Remember, you can press start to skip all the cutscenes.</p>

      <p>Return to the receptionist at the castle to complete the [Engineer Recruit] sidequest and receive <Tag type="gold">3000 G</Tag>. Then, head downstairs and talk to <Tag type="char">Meese</Tag> at the laboratory to complete the [Red-Letter Day] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="weapon">P.Thauma Spear</Tag> (ATK+23/DEF+2, equip on <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag>). Continue the plot as before, then take the elevator up to the <Tag type="place">3rd Floor</Tag> and talk to Lt. General <Tag type="char">Raul</Tag> at his office on the right.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Through Lazvil">
        <p>Afterwards, leave <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag> and head south to <Tag type="place">Lazvil Hills</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Silver Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Silver Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Alistel Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Pawn Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Rosch:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">P.Thauma Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Silver Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 14 -->
